"u1\\\",\\\"u3\\\",\\\"u9\\\",\\\"u17\\\",\\\"u18\\\"],\\n      \\\"status\\\":\\\"AMBIGUOUS\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"dimension\\\":\\\"exceptions\\\",\\n      \\\"explanation\\\":\\\"No express legacy-case, outage or enhancement-delay exception appears. Existing-channel acceptance attaches to the parallel run. 'Where practicable' attaches to SFC review and enhancement, not compulsory routing.\\\",\\n      \\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u4\\\",\\\"u7\\\",\\\"u11\\\"],\\n      \\\"status\\\":\\\"PROPOSED\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"dimension\\\":\\\"modality\\\",\\n      \\\"explanation\\\":\\\"'Must' requires covered submissions to use e-IP; 'can also' permits fee settlement. Monitoring, planned integration and continued enhancement describe SFC activities without independently imposing additional submission or payment duties.\\\",\\n      \\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u1\\\",\\\"u6\\\",\\\"u7\\\",\\\"u9\\\",\\\"u11\\\"],\\n      \\\"status\\\":\\\"PROPOSED\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"dimension\\\":\\\"time\\\",\\n      \\\"explanation\\\":\\\"The revised parallel run ends on 29 November 2024 and compulsory routing starts on 30 November 2024. The earlier 29 October endpoint is superseded. The event determining submission date, including dispatch versus accepted receipt, is unspecified.\\\",\\n      \\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u1\\\",\\\"u3\\\",\\\"u4\\\",\\\"u7\\\",\\\"u9\\\"],\\n      \\\"status\\\":\\\"AMBIGUOUS\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"dimension\\\":\\\"dependencies\\\",\\n      \\\"explanation\\\":\\\"The earlier launch circular is referenced but unavailable, and external-authorities.24ec50 is missing. Operational timing, migration rules and any externally authorized exceptions cannot be resolved from this packet. The supplied comparison diagnostics contain no counterexample valuations and establish only incomparable fact bindings.\\\",\\n      \\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u3\\\",\\\"u11\\\"],\\n      \\\"status\\\":\\\"AMBIGUOUS\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"questions\\\": [\\n    \\\"What provisions in the unavailable launch circular or operational guidance determine whether legacy-case follow-ups constitute submissions?\\\",\\n    \\\"Which event fixes submission_date, and what timing convention applies to transmission attempts spanning the transition?\\\",\\n    \\\"Can the five incomparable comparisons be supplied with their fact definitions and concrete valuations so that they can be tested against the same selected control?\\\",\\n    \\\"Do the missing authorities establish any outage or migration exception? None is established by the supplied text.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"readings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"assumptions\\\": [\\n        \\\"The control is evaluated for one identified application or submission, not for whole-institution compliance.\\\",\\n        \\\"Extending the parallel run extends its existing-channel acceptance through 29 November 2024.\\\",\\n        \\\"The supplied submission date is established under the applicable timing convention; this packet does not define that convention.\\\",\\n        \\\"Product and communication classification is supplied with professional judgment where needed.\\\",\\n        \\\"Missing operational guidance is not treated as evidence that an exception exists or that none could exist outside this packet.\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"citations\\\": [\\n        {\\n          \\\"quote\\\":\\\"After the extended period, applications and submissions of investment products administered by the Investment Products Division (IPD)1 must be submitted to IPD via e-IP from 30 November 2024.\\\",\\n          \\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u1\\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"quote\\\":\\\"processing new product applications and post-authorisation/registration submissions to IPD.\\\",\\n          \\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u3\\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"quote\\\":\\\"During this period, the SFC continues to accept applications and submissions via existing channels.\\\",\\n          \\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u4\\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"quote\\\":\\\"To facilitate these enhancements, the SFC will extend the parallel run period of e-IP by one month to 29 November 2024.\\\",\\n          \\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u7\\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"quote\\\":\\\"The current submission requests from IPD via the IP E-submission system will be integrated into e-IP, including reporting of net asset values, large redemptions and suspensions of dealing.\\\",\\n          \\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u9\\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"quote\\\":\\\"In addition, e-IP users can also settle recurring annual fees associated with relevant investment products through the new system.\\\",\\n          \\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u9\\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"quote\\\":\\\"The SFC will continue to review and enhance the operation of e-IP where practicable.\\\",\\n          \\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u11\\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"quote\\\":\\\"1 Investment-linked assurance schemes, mandatory provident fund products, open-ended fund companies, paper gold schemes, pooled retirement funds, real estate investment trusts, unit trusts and mutual funds and unlisted structured investment products.\\\",\\n          \\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u17\\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"quote\\\":\\\"2 Web-based INteGrated Service.\\\",\\n          \\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u18\\\"\\n        }\\n      ],\\n      \\\"distinction\\\":\\\"Retain the parent's mandatory-route reading with explicit evidentiary limits. A covered submission using an existing non-e-IP channel on 29 November is outside this mandatory control and within the extended acceptance period; the same item submitted on 30 November fails the route check. A fee payment alone does not establish coverage. Hypotheses that enhancements postpone the deadline, 'where practicable' excuses submitters, the full-adoption heading makes fee payment compulsory, or case initiation before transition creates grandfathering lack textual support. The uncited units add context and attribution, not a justified rival rule. The five INCOMPARABLE_FACT_BINDINGS diagnostics supply no substantive counterexample and therefore justify no change to fact meanings. The strongest remaining uncertainty is the classification and timing of legacy-case follow-ups.\\\",\\n      \\\"family\\\":\\\"time\\\",\\n      \\\"formalization\\\":{\\n        \\\"facts\\\":[\\n          {\\n            \\\"meaning\\\":\\\"The identified item is an application or submission to IPD concerning an investment product administered by IPD, interpreted with the product categories in footnote 1. Optional fee payment alone does not establish this classification.\\\",\\n            \\\"name\\\":\\\"covered_submission\\\",\\n            \\\"requires_judgment\\\":true,\\n            \\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u1\\\",\\\"u3\\\",\\\"u9\\\",\\\"u17\\\"],\\n            \\\"type\\\":\\\"bool\\\",\\n            \\\"unit\\\":\\\"Boolean\\\"\\n          },\\n          {\\n            \\\"meaning\\\":\\\"The Gregorian date on which the identified application or submission is treated as submitted under the applicable timing convention. Dispatch-versus-receipt treatment is not specified in the packet.\\\",\\n            \\\"name\\\":\\\"submission_date\\\",\\n            \\\"requires_judgment\\\":true,\\n            \\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u1\\\",\\\"u4\\\",\\\"u7\\\",\\\"u9\\\"],\\n            \\\"type\\\":\\\"date\\\",\\n            \\\"unit\\\":\\\"Gregorian calendar date\\\"\\n          },\\n          {\\n            \\\"meaning\\\":\\\"The identified application or submission was submitted to IPD via e-IP.\\\",\\n            \\\"name\\\":\\\"submitted_via_e_ip\\\",\\n            \\\"requires_judgment\\\":false,\\n            \\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u1\\\",\\\"u9\\\"],\\n            \\\"type\\\":\\\"bool\\\",\\n            \\\"unit\\\":\\\"Boolean\\\"\\n          